Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260418191737.10289-1-devnexen@gmail.com
Signed-off-by: David Carlier <devnexen@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Steven Rostedt <rostedt@goodmis.org>

Here is the root cause:
(1) the list traversal races with `list_del_rcu()` in `eventfs_remove_rec()`, causing list corruption; (2) `eventfs_inode` objects are freed via SRCU, but `rcu_read_lock()` does not extend an SRCU grace period, leading to use-after-free; (3) attribute writes to `ei->attr` race with `eventfs_set_attr()`, which holds `eventfs_mutex`. The missing `eventfs_mutex` and SRCU read lock allowed these races.

Here is the patch:

 static void eventfs_set_attrs(struct eventfs_inode *ei, bool update_uid, kuid_t uid,
 			      bool update_gid, kgid_t gid, int level)
 {
 	struct eventfs_inode *ei_child;

+	lockdep_assert_held(&eventfs_mutex);
+
 	/* Update events/<system>/<event> */
 	if (WARN_ON_ONCE(level > 3))
 		return;

 	if (update_uid) {
 		ei->attr.mode &= ~EVENTFS_SAVE_UID;
 		ei->attr.uid = uid;
 	}

 	if (update_gid) {
 		ei->attr.mode &= ~EVENTFS_SAVE_GID;
 		ei->attr.gid = gid;
 	}

 	list_for_each_entry(ei_child, &ei->children, list) {
 		eventfs_set_attrs(ei_child, update_uid, uid, update_gid, gid, level + 1);
 	}

 	if (!ei->entry_attrs)
 		return;

 	for (int i = 0; i < ei->nr_entries; i++) {
 		if (update_uid) {
 			ei->entry_attrs[i].mode &= ~EVENTFS_SAVE_UID;
 			ei->entry_attrs[i].uid = uid;
 		}
 		if (update_gid) {
 			ei->entry_attrs[i].mode &= ~EVENTFS_SAVE_GID;
 			ei->entry_attrs[i].gid = gid;
 		}
 	}

 }

+
+int eventfs_remount_lock(void)
+{
+	mutex_lock(&eventfs_mutex);
+	return srcu_read_lock(&eventfs_srcu);
+}
+
+void eventfs_remount_unlock(int srcu_idx)
+{
+	srcu_read_unlock(&eventfs_srcu, srcu_idx);
+	mutex_unlock(&eventfs_mutex);
+}


